ACC-014 — Engineering Intent

Document ID: ACC-014
Title: Engineering Intent
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines Engineering Intent, the objective that directs engineering cognition within the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

Engineering Intent establishes the desired engineering outcome that guides Engineering Observation, Engineering Understanding, Engineering Reasoning, Engineering Capability, and Decision Support.

It ensures that engineering cognition remains purposeful, relevant, and aligned with engineering objectives.

2. Scope

This specification applies to all engineering cognition performed within Atlas.

Engineering Intent may represent objectives such as:

Design
Analysis
Validation
Optimization
Inspection
Compliance verification
Risk assessment
Failure investigation
Cost estimation
Quantity estimation
Planning
Simulation
Prediction
Monitoring
Maintenance
Decision support

Engineering Intent applies to both human-initiated and autonomous engineering workflows.

3. Canonical Definition

Engineering Intent is the explicitly defined engineering objective that directs and constrains engineering cognition toward achieving a desired engineering outcome.

Engineering Intent defines what Atlas is trying to accomplish, not how it accomplishes it.

4. Characteristics

Engineering Intent SHALL possess the following characteristics.

4.1 Explicit

Engineering Intent SHALL be explicitly defined before initiating engineering cognition whenever practical.

4.2 Goal-Oriented

Engineering Intent SHALL identify a specific engineering objective.

4.3 Context-Dependent

Engineering Intent SHALL be interpreted within the applicable Engineering Context.

4.4 Traceable

Engineering Intent SHALL remain traceable throughout the engineering cognition lifecycle.

4.5 Stable

Engineering Intent SHOULD remain stable during a reasoning session unless explicitly revised.

4.6 Measurable

Engineering Intent SHOULD enable evaluation of whether the intended engineering objective has been achieved.

4.7 Evolvable

Engineering Intent MAY evolve as engineering requirements or stakeholder objectives change.

