Engineering Intent:

Directs Engineering Observation.
Focuses Engineering Reasoning.
Determines applicable Engineering Capabilities.
Shapes Decision Support.
Does not alter Engineering Reality.
6. Responsibilities

Engineering Intent is responsible for:

Defining engineering objectives.
Guiding engineering cognition.
Prioritizing relevant engineering information.
Aligning engineering reasoning with desired outcomes.
Supporting evaluation of engineering results.
Maintaining objective consistency throughout engineering workflows.
7. Normative Requirements

Engineering Intent SHALL:

Define a clear engineering objective.
Be associated with Engineering Context.
Guide Engineering Reasoning and Engineering Capability selection.
Remain traceable throughout engineering cognition.
Be reviewed when engineering objectives materially change.

Atlas SHALL NOT initiate autonomous engineering reasoning without a defined Engineering Intent.

8. Non-Goals

Engineering Intent does not:

Represent Engineering Reality.
Replace Engineering Context.
Perform Engineering Reasoning.
Define Engineering Knowledge.
Guarantee successful engineering outcomes.
Authorize engineering decisions.
9. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY define intent hierarchies, intent decomposition, intent conflict resolution, multi-objective engineering optimization, and collaborative intent management without changing the canonical definition established by this specification.